# PLE program: per-measurement intermediates. These WERE ignored, on the reasoning that
# consolidate.py folds them into the committed CSVs so only the CSVs need tracking. That reasoning
# has one hole and it cost real work: consolidate.py REBUILDS the committed files from these, so a
# checkout without them produces a valid, much smaller CSV and exits 0. Run in a fresh worktree it
# cut ple_results.csv from 459 rows to 180 and layer_freeing_results.csv from 124 to 46, and only
# `git status` showed it. There is now a guard that aborts on any dropped row -- but a guard that
# fires means work stops, and the honest fix is for the inputs to be present.
#
# They total 18 KB. Tracking them makes the repository able to rebuild its own results.
#
# results/ablations/ple_accounting.csv          } all now TRACKED
# results/ablations/ple_cal_stack.csv           }
# results/ablations/ple_calib_meta*.json        }
# results/ablations/ple_coverage.csv            }
# results/ablations/ple_heldout.csv             }
# results/ablations/joint_free.csv              }
# results/ablations/layer_damage.csv            }
# results/ablations/ple_locus.csv               }
# results/ablations/ple_parity.csv              }
# results/ablations/ple_row_norms.csv           }
# results/ablations/ple_trainfree_and_buckets.csv }
results/ablations/ple_ladder.csv
